{
  "summary": "Moves the `getblocktemplate` block template cache out of function-local static variables in `rpc/mining.cpp` and into `BlockTemplateManager`. Cached templates now share the lifetime of the node context rather than the process, and member accesses are annotated with `GUARDED_BY(::cs_main)`. The lookup replaces raw `CBlockIndex*` caching with active chain tip hash comparisons and adds unit tests for cache invalidation, rebuild intervals, and failed build retries.",
  "problem": "Process-wide function-local statics in `getblocktemplate` allow cached `CBlockIndex*` pointers to outlive their owning `ChainstateManager` in test environments. In addition, the static cache lacks compile-time thread-safety annotations for `cs_main` and cannot be unit-tested in isolation.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description explains the motivation: 'live as long as the process, so the cached CBlockIndex* can outlive its ChainstateManager (as in unit tests); rely on cs_main being held, which nothing checks; can't be unit tested.'",
    "Linked tracking issue #33758 identifies removing remaining global states in block template management as an open milestone."
  ],
